#: ../../docstring of text_filter.TextFilterAssetsStandard:3
msgid ""
"Both arguments accept either an already-compiled regex or its source as a"
" string: the real compilation happens inside the native type, so from a "
"compiled pattern only its source is taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of text_filter.TextFilterInvestmentsStandard:3
msgid ""
"`dash_as_zero` is the same flag expression the structured level writes in"
" its `Interpret dash as zero` column — `\"MARKET_VALUE | "
"PERC_NET_ASSETS\"`, `\"ALL\"` — and `None` is the empty set, so an "
"unstructured format that says nothing behaves as it always has."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of text_filter.TextFilterInvestmentsStandard:7
msgid ""
"`remove_from_fund_regexes` is the `Remove from fund` column: patterns cut"
" out of the fund's name before it becomes the sub-fund's identity — the "
"`(continued)` of a continuation page, or a footnote mark at its end "
"(`R16`), `r\"\\s*[*]*\\s*$\"`. It accepts one pattern or an iterable of "
"them, as a string or an already-compiled `re.Pattern` — from a compiled "
"one only its source is taken, since the compilation happens inside the "
"native type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of text_filter.TextFilterSfdrSignStandard:4
msgid ""
"**A divergence absorbed here:** a single argument mixes literal strings "
"and already-compiled patterns, while the native type wants them "
"separated, the first going through a plain substring replacement and the "
"second through the regex engine. The sorting happens here, and the "
"relative order within each of the two groups is preserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of text_filter.TextFilterSfdrSignStandard:9
msgid ""
"`fund_block_type` names the block the fund's own `pdf_extract` pipe "
"produced, and defaults to `FUND_NAME`, which is what "
"`PdfExtractLabelledValueStandard` is normally told to emit."
msgstr ""

